## Completion and direct review

Implemented provider-neutral automatic heartbeats and interruption recovery behavior:
- lifecycle ownership renews before broker delivery extension;
- renewal can rotate fencing tokens used by later progress and completion;
- heartbeat activity settles before terminal mutation;
- lifecycle rejection, delivery-extension failure, callback errors, or unsettled shutdown cause release without completion, failure, or acknowledgement;
- executors can observe ownership loss cooperatively;
- the standard scheduler uses a bounded daemon-thread shutdown;
- tests use deterministic manual scheduling and clocks.

Direct review required synchronization of ownership-loss publication and ensured process-level exceptions are not swallowed.

Validation:
- python -m behave tests/command_worker/features → 10 scenarios and 52 steps passed
- python -m pytest -q tests/command_worker → 44 passed
- python -m pytest -q plexus/cli/shared/command_dispatch_test.py plexus/cli/shared/command_tasks_test.py → 17 passed
- ruff check plexus/command_worker tests/command_worker → passed
- ruff format --check plexus/command_worker tests/command_worker → passed
- provider-boundary check → no forbidden imports

Provider adapters, durable attempt history, cancellation, deployment draining, subprocess isolation, and dashboard integration remain follow-up work.
